      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A mod used to basically enable this sort of functionality.\n\nBeing able to block avatars based on specific parameters would be amazing, especially like you said with VRAM. I'd be able to just set it to 100 MB and not really worry about my VRAM filling up. \n\nEven having custom presets for settings would be nice. Like being able to toggle between \"basic public\" and \"dense event\".",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-02-17T17:43:40.300Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently rating is hard set by vrchat, so no matter what hardware you have and what kind of worlds you join you are forced to use the global definition of excellent/good/medium/poor/very poor.\n\nI feel like for many of us this basically makes some or all of this ranks completely useless, like i can't use performance limiter because 90% of people I'm around will disappear.  \n\nI would want to be able to use performance limiter as it can disable certain components like lights past the limit without disabling the avatar, but I can't do that if I can't control the other values, as right now it will just hide everyone with more than 70k polys for example.\n\nIf I could define in settings or at least a simple config file what I consider good/poor/etc I could define own limits that make sense for my hardware and instances I join. Even better if I could have multiple profiles of these settings so I can easily switch when I'm just hanging out vs joining 40+ people event. For example I could set my custom limits allowing for 200k poly poor avatars with 2 lights, 2 cloths, 30 textures and 200mb vram, and then set my performance limiter based on that - as I know that in the instance I'm in this should keep me running just fine. \n\nThis would also solve many other feature requests about certain performance rank elements, like recent vram limit: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/max-avatar-vram-size as I could just set one of ratings to match my needs\n\nAlternative or supplementary idea would be to introduce a global performance budget, allowing you to limit how many polys/textures/lights/etc you want to be able to render at once - no matter how many avatars they are coming from.: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/local-avatar-performance-budget",
